cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Catalog-bound authority: lifecycle control over records you do not store"
abstract: >-
  An experiment report on governing AI-agent memory held in an external store.
  Ownership is split by role rather than by location: the provider keeps content,
  embeddings and search, while a local catalog keeps identity, exact version,
  provenance, lifecycle status and a keyed fingerprint. Policy runs before any
  content fetch. Two properties follow: a denied record is never fetched, and
  revocation works without the ability to delete. Verified as an executable
  matrix of ten checks against an in-process fixture, with limitations stated.
